Sigma reimplements subscription login from the public behavior of the
official CLIs and from the MIT-licensed CLIProxyAPI project. It does not
copy source from sub2api (LGPL-3.0).

Adapted protocol notes, with attribution:

- ChatGPT / Codex OAuth client id, authorize and token URLs, PKCE parameters,
  and the Codex Responses endpoint headers. Public client
  `app_EMoamEEZ73f0CkXaXp7hrann` ships in openai/codex (Apache-2.0) and in
  router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI (MIT).
  https://github.com/openai/codex
  https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI

- Claude Code OAuth client id, authorize and token URLs, and the JSON token
  request. Documented from router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI (MIT) and public Claude
  Code traces.
  https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI

- Gemini CLI installed-app OAuth and the Code Assist (`cloudcode-pa`) calls.
  The client id and secret are published in google-gemini/gemini-cli
  (Apache-2.0). They are not copied into this tree, because GitHub secret
  scanning rejects them. Set SIGMA_GEMINI_CLIENT_ID and
  SIGMA_GEMINI_CLIENT_SECRET from that project.
  https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli
  https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI

- Grok CLI OAuth client id, OIDC issuer, and the CLI chat proxy base URL.
  Documented from router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI (MIT).
  https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI

